    detail: The comparison notes that one page costs one credit, JSON extraction adds four credits, and pages returning 403 or 404 still consume one credit; it also cites ScrapeBadger pay-as-you-go at $0.15 per 1,000 credits and Firecrawl Standard at $0.83 per 1,000 credits.
- [W7] Use-Apify reported that LLM-based extraction adds per-page inference costs of $0.001 to $0.01 depending on model and page length, with slower throughput than selector-based extraction. (source: use-apify.com, 2026-03)
    detail: The guide says selectors still win for high-volume, price-sensitive pipelines, while LLM extraction is increasingly used for variable layouts, one-off extractions and rapid prototyping.
