t has become."]}, "sections": [{"sop": "report_context", "heading": "Report Context for the Digital Marketing Software Market", "paragraphs": ["The size of the digital marketing software market puts it among the larger software categories, and the forecast points to steady expansion rather than a sudden spike. CMI's report values the market at USD 17.85 billion in 2026 and projects USD 37.94 billion by 2033. That works out to a compound annual growth rate of 11.2% across the period, a pace that roughly doubles the market in seven years. The digital marketing software market growth rate rests on businesses of all sizes moving more of their promotion onto software they pay for by subscription. A steady double-digit pace like this usually means demand is broadening rather than concentrating in a few big buyers."]}, {"sop": "trends", "heading": "What are the latest trends in digital marketing software?", "paragraphs": ["Three shifts stand out in the trends shaping the digital marketing software market: artificial intelligence is making campaigns sharper, buyers want one tool that covers every channel, and live data is helping companies keep customers longer.\n- Artificial intelligence and machine learning now drive personalisation and campaign results, and CMI's report credits AI users with conversion rates up to 30% higher in 2026.\n- Omnichannel marketing pushes companies toward tools that pull cross-channel data into one view, and early adopters saw a 25% increase in omnichannel marketing software ROI increase, according to the CMI report.\n- Real-time analytics lets teams spot unhappy customers early, and CMI's report links adoption of real-time analytics to a 20% cut in customer churn.\nThe tool count has exploded alongside these shifts. The marketing technology landscape grew from 150 solutions in 2011 to 15,384, gtm8020.com reported in January 2026, with 2,489 new tools qualifying in 2025. The average enterprise now runs more than 90 marketing technology tools at