      "question": "What are the latest trends in digital marketing software?",
      "answer": "The biggest trends are AI-driven personalization, omnichannel data unification, real-time analytics and the rise of AI platforms as a referral channel. AI users achieved up to 30% higher conversion rates in 2026, and early omnichannel adopters saw a 25% increase in ROI, while real-time analytics adoption cuts customer churn by 20%. The marketing technology landscape has grown from 150 solutions in 2011 to 15,384 solutions, a 9% increase from 14,106, according to gtm8020.com in January 2026, and a Gartner survey reported by cmonewsdesk.com in July 2026 found 78% of CMOs feel unprepared for the future of marketing technology."
    },
    {
      "question": "How is AI changing digital marketing software?",
      "answer": "AI is reshaping digital marketing software by making personalization and campaign execution more automated, and by turning AI platforms into new customer touchpoints. Salesforce made AI agents touchpoints in the customer journey as part of its Agentforce launch, tying them into its revenue engine and attribution models, according to Forrester Blogs in October 2026. Interviews with 15 global CMOs surfaced five priorities reshaping marketing leadership in an AI-driven world, including transforming with and for AI and developing new metrics for zero-click AI platforms, according to MIT Sloan Management Review in September 2026."
    },
    {
      "question": "Who are the top players in the digital marketing software market?",
      "answer": "The key players named in the report are Adobe, Oracle, IBM, ZOHO, Cheetah Digital, SAS Institute, HubSpot, Sprout Social, ActiveCampaign and Salesforce. Salesforce also agreed to acquire marketing technology platform Braze for $47.50 a share in cash, valuing Braze at $5.66 billion including debt, CNBC reported in October 2026."
    }
  ]
}
